[1m[38;5;231mWhen should a reminder fire relative to a task's due time?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [ ] [38;5;153mDue time + global lead (Recommended)[39m
  [38;5;246mFires at due time, and optionally N minutes earlier via one global setting. No per-task field or UI. Extends cleanly [39m
  [38;5;246mto per-task later via a nullable override.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m [ ] Exactly at due time
  [38;5;246mAbsolute simplest: dueAt fires it, nothing else stored. No warning ahead of time.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m [ ] Per-task reminder time
  [38;5;246mEvery task carries its own reminder time. Full control, but adds a field and a control in the editor on day one.[39m
  [38;5;246m4.[39m [ ] Keep nagging when overdue
  [38;5;246mRe-notify on an interval until the task is completed. Independent of the choices above; effective, and easy to find [39m
  [38;5;246mirritating.[39m
